A thread taken off a ring while it is the oldest stays the ring's head.
The next signal would wake a thread that is no longer waiting,
and the next switch run one that is already running;
a queue holds only threads in the state it is for.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-grain32 fuzz-work test qemu-replay
Report: queue holds a thread it is not for

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -63,9 +63,6 @@ static void ring_remove(paddr_t *head, struct thread *t)
     } else {
         ((struct thread *)p2v(t->queue_prev))->queue_next = t->queue_next;
         ((struct thread *)p2v(t->queue_next))->queue_prev = t->queue_prev;
-        if (*head == v2p(t)) {
-            *head = t->queue_next;
-        }
     }
     t->queue_next = t->queue_prev = 0;
 }
